/-
# `BridgeSquare/cuspPair_surjective.lean` — surjectivity of the cusp pair `F_k = (H_k τ, H_k π)`

The cusp pair `F_k = cuspPair k = biprod.lift (H_k τ) (H_k π)` is the Mayer–Vietoris map of the
cover `M̂ = A ∪ B` in the cusp vocabulary (`Submission/Work/NOTES_LEAD_aspherical_bridge.md` §2).
This file proves that it is **surjective** in the three degrees `k = 1, 2, 3` in which the models
of `Work.HomologyMV` are non-trivial, from the two geometric inputs

* **(c)** `H_k(τ)` is surjective for `k = 1, 2, 3` (`Work.BridgeSquare.cuspMap_surjective`), and
* **(a)** `H_k(s_v) = 0` for `k = 1, 2` (`Work.BridgeSquare.SubtorusNull`),

together with the two formal facts `H_k(π) ≫ H_k(secMap) = 1` (the section of the projection,
`cuspPair_P_surjective`) and `H_3(⊔_v T²_v) = 0` (the tori are surfaces).

## The argument

Write `F = H(τ)`, `P = H(π)` and let `s = secMap0 : ⊔_v T²_v → ⊔_v (∂[-1,1]² × T²_v)` be the
section at a basepoint of the square boundary, so that `P ≫ H(s) = 1` and `F ≫ H(s) = 0` (**a**,
by `secMap0_comp_cuspMap_eq_zero` below).  Given `(a, c)` in `H_k(M̄) ⊞ H_k(⊔_v T²_v)`, choose
`x₂` with `F x₂ = a` (**c**) and put

`x := x₂ + H(s) (c - P x₂)`.

Then `P x = P x₂ + (c - P x₂) = c` and `F x = a + 0 = a`; hence `F = (F, P)` is surjective.

## The two ingredients

* **`H(s) (H(⊔_v T²_v)) ⊆ ker F`.**  The homology `H_k(⊔_v T²_v)` of the disjoint union is
  generated by the images of its pieces `T²_v`: the chain-level splitting of the singular chains
  over the finite disjoint open cover of the five tori (`Work.BridgeSquare.sigmaOpenCoverChain`,
  degreewise `∑ π_i ∘ ι_i = 1`) gives the identity

  `1 = ∑_v H(eC.inv ≫ π_v) ∘ H(incl_v)`

  on `H_k(⊔_v T²_v)`, and the inclusion of the `v`-th piece is the inverse of the canonical
  homeomorphism `T²_v ≅ {⟨v,·⟩}` followed by `secT v`, so that (a) says that `F ≫ H(s)` kills the
  image of every `H(incl_v)`, whence `F ≫ H(s) = 0`.
* **`k = 3`.**  Here (a) is not available (the hypotheses only cover `k = 1, 2`), but
  `H_3(T²_v) = 0`: the standard `Δ`-structure of the torus has `rankT2 3 = 0`
  (`Work.PieceHomology.eT2_torus2`).  Hence `H_k(Fn v) = 0` in degree `3` as well, and the same
  argument applies.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.BridgeSquare.CuspSection
